message: "If you use this software or its data, please cite the paper below."
title: "Reflexive Descent to Minimal Seeds in the Kreuzer–Skarke List: code, data and checks"
abstract: >-
  Code, data and independent checks for the paper "Reflexive Descent to
  Minimal Seeds in the Kreuzer–Skarke List". The paper proves that every
  reflexive polytope can be shrunk to a minimal seed through reflexive
  polytopes one cover at a time, that no such descent in dimension four has
  more than 348 steps, so that the conjecture of a uniform transition depth
  holds with D = 349, and that the largest transition depths in dimensions two
  and three are 5 and 11. The archive holds the joint distribution of point
  counts over the 473,800,776 four-dimensional reflexive polytopes, the pair
  bounds and a longest chain, the cover relation in dimensions two and three,
  a certified descent of the largest polytope, and 68 independent checks in C,
  C++, Python, Julia, Macaulay2 and shell with 18 Lean 4 theorems.
